<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<FlexiPage xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        THIS NOTE LIVES IN A COMMENT INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT - a comment placed ABOVE <FlexiPage>
        breaks `sf` deploy at source conversion with a misleading "unable to find matching parent
        xml file" error.

        =====================================================================
        🔴 2026-08-27 - ACQUISITION SIDE NOW ALSO CONVERTED, FINISHING THIS PAGE. Both
        Contract_Review__c.Advance_Stage entries described below (2026-08-26 edit) are REMOVED.
        Replaced by three acquisition entries: reused page entries on Move_to_Negotiation
        (Draft -> Negotiation) and Move_to_Signed (Negotiation -> Signed), and a new
        Move_to_Executed (Signed -> Executed). The Move_to_Executed record-type pin is the
        highest-consequence single criterion in this whole change — see its own comment below.
        RENDERER BEHAVIOUR ON THE ACQUISITION SIDE IS NOT PROVEN FROM THIS REPO — see
        design-requirements.md §7.2, in particular the negative check that a disposition PSA at
        its 'Signed' terminal shows NO 'Executed' button.
        =====================================================================

        =====================================================================
        🔴 2026-08-26 - "ADVANCE STAGE" IS REPLACED BY NAMED PER-HOP BUTTONS ON THE DISPOSITION
        SIDE ONLY. USER DECISION: "we don't need a quick action named 'Advance Stage'; instead we
        need the NEXT STAGE NAME."
        =====================================================================

        TWO NEW ENTRIES, ONE PER HOP OF CONTRACT_REVIEW_DISPOSITION_NEXT_STAGE, each labelled with
        the status the click lands on: Move_to_Negotiation ("Negotiation", at Initial Draft) and
        Move_to_Signed ("Signed", at Negotiation). Both point at the SAME c/advanceRecordStage
        bundle the generic button uses - the target is derived server-side from the record's
        current status, per record type - so the label is a promise these rules keep, not anything
        the client sends.

        🔴 THE CRITERION IS Negotiation_Status__c, NOT Stage__c, ON EVERY ENTRY INCLUDING THE NEW
        ONES. Stage__c on this object is DERIVED and unwritable; CONFIG_BY_TYPE says so in as many
        words. A rule written against Stage__c here would look right and never fire.

        🔴 ACQUISITION IS UNCHANGED, AND THAT WAS THE CONSTRAINT. Both pre-existing Advance_Stage
        entries KEEP their two criteria - the Acquisition one still tests NE 'Executed', the
        disposition one still tests NE 'Signed', exactly as the 2026-08-21 amendment below left
        them - and each gains a third: {!Record.RecordType.DeveloperName} NE Disposition_PSA. Same
        construct and same operator as LOI_Record_Page's criterion 5, which was validated against
        usman-dpeg by a four-probe check-only control on 2026-08-21 (probe B is the one that
        matters: a bogus field placed BEHIND the RecordType hop was rejected BY NAME, so the
        validator resolved the reference rather than waving a string through). On an Acquisition_PSA
        row the new criterion is TRUE, so nothing an acquisition user sees moves; on a Master-typed
        row RecordType.DeveloperName reads BLANK and blank NE 'Disposition_PSA' is TRUE, so the
        button FAILS OPEN - the polarity code review forced on LOI_Record_Page (C2). The two NEW
        entries use EQUAL Disposition_PSA, which fails CLOSED on Master; correct for a
        disposition-only button.

        ⚠ IT TAKES THE CRITERION ON *BOTH* Advance_Stage ENTRIES, NOT JUST THE DISPOSITION-GATED
        ONE. The Acquisition_Deal_Actions entry has always rendered on a disposition PSA for
        anyone holding that permission (the accepted cosmetic residual this module records on
        NDA_Record_Page and LOI_Record_Page); left alone it would keep rendering "Advance Stage"
        beside the new named buttons. The disposition-gated entry is now dead on every row -
        criterion 1 wants the disposition persona, criterion 3 excludes the disposition record
        type - and is RETAINED rather than deleted, because this edit was scoped to adding
        criteria and deleting entries is how action bars have been emptied in this repo before.

        ⚠ BOTH SELL-SIDE LITERALS ARE SHARED WITH Acquisition_PSA. 'Negotiation' and 'Signed' are
        on both record types (the two sequences were split on 2026-08-14 but not made disjoint), so
        the record-type criterion on the new entries is load-bearing, not decorative: without it
        Move_to_Signed would render on an acquisition PSA at 'Negotiation'. 'Initial Draft' is
        disposition-only and is also DispositionStageEntryService's DISPOSITION_PSA_INITIAL_STATUS,
        so Move_to_Negotiation is the first button on a newly created sell-side PSA.

        ⚠ STILL NOT PROVEN FROM A REPO: RENDERER BEHAVIOUR. After deploying, a human must open
        (1) a disposition PSA at Initial Draft and at Negotiation and see exactly ONE
        correctly-named button and NO "Advance Stage", (2) an acquisition PSA at Draft /
        Negotiation / Signed and see "Advance Stage" unchanged with none of the new buttons, and
        (3) a Master-typed Contract Review, confirming "Advance Stage" survives. Direction (1)
        alone cannot distinguish a working rule from one the renderer ignores.

        NO PERMISSION SET CHANGED. The new criteria read the Disposition_Deal_Actions custom
        permission (no FLS to be missing), RecordType, and Negotiation_Status__c - measured
        present on both DPEG_Disposition_Edit and DPEG_Disposition_View.

        AMENDED 2026-08-21. The Disposition_Deal_Actions Advance_Stage visibilityRule below
        tested Negotiation_Status__c NE 'Executed', copied from the Acquisition_Deal_Actions
        entry above it when both were written against Disposition_PSA's then-terminal value
        'Executed'. The user changed Disposition_PSA's sequence directly in Setup the same day
        (see objects/Contract_Review__c/recordTypes/Disposition_PSA.recordType-meta.xml for the
        full record): the sell-side terminal is now 'Signed', and this record type can never
        equal 'Executed' again, which made the old criterion always-true on a disposition row -
        Advance Stage would have kept rendering past this record type's real terminal.
        FIXED: the Disposition_Deal_Actions entry now tests NE 'Signed'.
        ⚠ The Acquisition_Deal_Actions entry directly above is UNCHANGED and correctly still
        tests NE 'Executed' - Acquisition_PSA's terminal did not move.
    -->
    <flexiPageRegions>
        <itemInstances>
            <componentInstance>
                <componentInstanceProperties>
                    <name>actionNames</name>
                    <valueList>
                        <!-- 2026-08-27 — both Contract_Review__c.Advance_Stage entries that stood
                             here are REMOVED, finishing the "separate, deliberate step" the
                             disposition-side edits below called for (the disposition-gated entry
                             was already self-contradictory after the record-type criterion was
                             added — Disposition_Deal_Actions + NE 'Disposition_PSA' can never both
                             be true). Replaced by three acquisition entries: reused page entries on
                             Move_to_Negotiation (Draft -> Negotiation) and Move_to_Signed
                             (Negotiation -> Signed), and a new Move_to_Executed
                             (Signed -> Executed). All three carry
                             {!Record.RecordType.DeveloperName} NE 'Disposition_PSA' (NE, not EQUAL
                             'Acquisition_PSA' — fails OPEN on Master, matching
                             RecordStageAdvanceService's defaultTypeKey). -->
                        <valueListItems>
                            <value>Contract_Review__c.Move_to_Negotiation</value>
                            <visibilityRule>
                                <booleanFilter>1 AND 2 AND 3</booleanFilter>
                                <criteria>
                                    <leftValue>{!$Permission.CustomPermission.Acquisition_Deal_Actions}</leftValue>
                                    <operator>EQUAL</operator>
                                    <rightValue>true</rightValue>
                                </criteria>
                                <criteria>
                                    <leftValue>{!Record.RecordType.DeveloperName}</leftValue>
                                    <operator>NE</operator>
                                    <rightValue>Disposition_PSA</rightValue>
                                </criteria>
                                <criteria>
                                    <leftValue>{!Record.Negotiation_Status__c}</leftValue>
                                    <operator>EQUAL</operator>
                                    <rightValue>Draft</rightValue>
                                </criteria>
                            </visibilityRule>
                        </valueListItems>
                        <!-- REUSED ACTION: Contract_Review__c.Move_to_Signed already exists below
                             (disposition terminal button, Negotiation -> Signed). This is a second
                             page entry pointing at the same file for the acquisition hop
                             Negotiation -> Signed — SAME STAGE VALUE as the disposition entry,
                             separated ONLY by the inverted record-type operator. -->
                        <valueListItems>
                            <value>Contract_Review__c.Move_to_Signed</value>
                            <visibilityRule>
                                <booleanFilter>1 AND 2 AND 3</booleanFilter>
                                <criteria>
                                    <leftValue>{!$Permission.CustomPermission.Acquisition_Deal_Actions}</leftValue>
                                    <operator>EQUAL</operator>
                                    <rightValue>true</rightValue>
                                </criteria>
                                <criteria>
                                    <leftValue>{!Record.RecordType.DeveloperName}</leftValue>
                                    <operator>NE</operator>
                                    <rightValue>Disposition_PSA</rightValue>
                                </criteria>
                                <criteria>
                                    <leftValue>{!Record.Negotiation_Status__c}</leftValue>
                                    <operator>EQUAL</operator>
                                    <rightValue>Negotiation</rightValue>
                                </criteria>
                            </visibilityRule>
                        </valueListItems>
                        <!-- 🔴 THE RT PIN ON THIS ENTRY IS THE HIGHEST-CONSEQUENCE SINGLE CRITERION
                             IN THIS WHOLE CHANGE. 'Signed' is mid-sequence on Acquisition_PSA but
                             TERMINAL on Disposition_PSA, and 'Executed' is not even a value on the
                             Disposition_PSA record type. Negotiation_Status__c is a RESTRICTED
                             picklist whose record-type subset Apex DML enforces (measured
                             2026-08-21) — without this pin, a click on a completed sell-side PSA
                             would fail with an opaque INVALID_OR_NULL_FOR_RESTRICTED_PICKLIST
                             instead of never rendering the button at all. -->
                        <valueListItems>
                            <value>Contract_Review__c.Move_to_Executed</value>
                            <visibilityRule>
                                <booleanFilter>1 AND 2 AND 3</booleanFilter>
                                <criteria>
                                    <leftValue>{!$Permission.CustomPermission.Acquisition_Deal_Actions}</leftValue>
                                    <operator>EQUAL</operator>
                                    <rightValue>true</rightValue>
                                </criteria>
                                <criteria>
                                    <leftValue>{!Record.RecordType.DeveloperName}</leftValue>
                                    <operator>NE</operator>
                                    <rightValue>Disposition_PSA</rightValue>
                                </criteria>
                                <criteria>
                                    <leftValue>{!Record.Negotiation_Status__c}</leftValue>
                                    <operator>EQUAL</operator>
                                    <rightValue>Signed</rightValue>
                                </criteria>
                            </visibilityRule>
                        </valueListItems>
                        <!-- 'Executed' is the acquisition PSA's TERMINAL status — no button
                             follows it, per user decision #2 (no-next-step stages render nothing,
                             no hint text). -->
                        <valueListItems>
                            <value>Contract_Review__c.Move_to_Negotiation</value>
                            <visibilityRule>
                                <booleanFilter>1 AND 2 AND 3</booleanFilter>
                                <criteria>
                                    <leftValue>{!$Permission.CustomPermission.Disposition_Deal_Actions}</leftValue>
                                    <operator>EQUAL</operator>
                                    <rightValue>true</rightValue>
                                </criteria>
                                <criteria>
                                    <leftValue>{!Record.RecordType.DeveloperName}</leftValue>
                                    <operator>EQUAL</operator>
                                    <rightValue>Disposition_PSA</rightValue>
                                </criteria>
                                <criteria>
                                    <leftValue>{!Record.Negotiation_Status__c}</leftValue>
                                    <operator>EQUAL</operator>
                                    <rightValue>Initial Draft</rightValue>
                                </criteria>
                            </visibilityRule>
                        </valueListItems>
                        <valueListItems>
                            <value>Contract_Review__c.Move_to_Signed</value>
                            <visibilityRule>
                                <booleanFilter>1 AND 2 AND 3</booleanFilter>
                                <criteria>
                                    <leftValue>{!$Permission.CustomPermission.Disposition_Deal_Actions}</leftValue>
                                    <operator>EQUAL</operator>
                                    <rightValue>true</rightValue>
                                </criteria>
                                <criteria>
                                    <leftValue>{!Record.RecordType.DeveloperName}</leftValue>
                                    <operator>EQUAL</operator>
                                    <rightValue>Disposition_PSA</rightValue>
                                </criteria>
                                <criteria>
                                    <leftValue>{!Record.Negotiation_Status__c}</leftValue>
                                    <operator>EQUAL</operator>
                                    <rightValue>Negotiation</rightValue>
                                </criteria>
                            </visibilityRule>
                        </valueListItems>
                    </valueList>
                </componentInstanceProperties>
                <componentInstanceProperties>
                    <name>collapsed</name>
                    <value>false</value>
                </componentInstanceProperties>
                <componentInstanceProperties>
                    <name>enableActionsConfiguration</name>
                    <value>true</value>
                </componentInstanceProperties>
                <componentInstanceProperties>
                    <name>hideChatterActions</name>
                    <value>false</value>
                </componentInstanceProperties>
                <componentInstanceProperties>
                    <name>hideSlackAction</name>
                    <value>false</value>
                </componentInstanceProperties>
                <componentName>force:highlightsPanel</componentName>
                <identifier>highlightsPanel</identifier>
            </componentInstance>
        </itemInstances>
